From 401c334cde1081d10916154beaea436f2dd68a43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Red <235753003+ban-red@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:32:43 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] [dxvk] Negotiate a modifier where a linear dma-buf export
 can't render

A texture created with DXVK_D3D11_RESOURCE_MISC_LINEAR_EXPORT may only
use DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR. On NVIDIA the linear layout has no
VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_BIT, so a render target with that
flag finds no modifier and creation fails. A paravirtual display
driver sets the flag on Windows' scanout surfaces.

When the linear-only search finds nothing, search again without the
restriction and log once that a tiled modifier is used instead. The
consumer must then import with the modifier, as QEMU's virtio-gpu
dma-buf scanout does when it is given one.

Most of the diff is the modifier loop moving into a lambda.
